Debezium JSON parsing: temporal strings, typed arrays, source-type options.

Flink CDC's pipeline debezium-json declares temporal columns with the numeric
debezium temporal types (MicroTimestamp, Timestamp, Date, MicroTime) but
serializes the value as a formatted datetime string. Upstream
DebeziumSchemaUtils.transformRawValue calls Long.parseLong on that string and
throws NumberFormatException. This parses the string and re-formats it, so the
typed TIMESTAMP, DATE and TIME columns stay.

DebeziumJsonRecordParser keeps the element type of ARRAY columns and passes
their original JSON on, so arrays no longer degrade to STRING. It also
republishes the `__lago.source.type` column parameter that leg 1 sets as the
table option `lago.source-type.<column>`, which leg 3 reads (see patch 0002).

Moved from getlago/lago-infrastructure images/flink-paimon/patches/, where the
classes were recompiled over the released jar.

